// The monitor, as a sprite.
//
// The Stage's pen belongs to a sprite, so the screen needs one of its own, and
// this is it: hidden, with a one-pixel costume it never wears, drawing the
// graphics card's scanout whenever the card has a frame the monitor has not
// drawn. What "has not drawn" means is the panel's: the indexed one is the
// frame the guest committed and the board latched, and the direct colour one
// is the guest's own memory, read at the rate a pen can draw it.
//
// It is a separate target from the machine for the same reason `monitor.rav`
// is in the ARM build: the machine's thread is `warp` from one end of a slice
// to the other, and Scratch runs the targets in turn, so the drawing happens
// in the gap the machine leaves when it hands the frame back.

use rvmonitor::efb;

sprite "Monitor" {
    costume "blank" = "assets/blank.svg";

    on flag_clicked {
        looks::hide();
    }

    on broadcast_received("Monitor.run") {
        pen::set_pen_size_to(1);
        forever {
            monitor_frames += 1;
            monitor_draw();
        }
    }
}
